.TH PYLOADER 8 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
pyloader \- DarqOS loader for Python executables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyloader
.I p-kernel-port dpid parent-dpid executable-path
.br
.B pyloader
.RB { help | \-h | \-? | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyloader
runs a Python executable as a DarqOS process.
It is normally started by
.BR pkernel (8)
in response to a
.B spawn_process
p-call, and is not meant to be run by hand.
.PP
.B pyloader
connects to the p-kernel on the loopback interface at
.IR p-kernel-port ,
and sends a RUN_REQUEST message for
.IR dpid .
Once the p-kernel accepts it with a RUN_RESPONSE,
.B pyloader
imports
.I main.py
from
.I executable-path
and calls its
.B darq_main()
function, with no arguments, on the main thread.
The application owns the main thread, so it can use toolkits, such as
Qt, that require it, and it receives signals.
.PP
A second, I/O, thread runs an event loop that carries p-calls from the
application to the p-kernel and delivers the replies.
A synchronous p-call blocks the application until its reply arrives.
Completion callbacks, and messages delivered to the listener set by
.BR init_cb() ,
are called on the application's own event loop, as given to
.B init()
or
.BR init_cb() .
The process's
.B getpid()
and
.B getppid()
are answered locally from
.I dpid
and
.IR parent-dpid .
.PP
The host process title is set to
.BI darq- dpid
to make it easy to find with
.BR ps (1).
.SS Termination
.B pyloader
exits when the application's
.B darq_main()
finishes, or when the p-kernel delivers a
.B kill_process
for this dpid.
.PP
When
.B darq_main()
finishes, its exit status is reported to the p-kernel in an EXITED
message:
.IP \(bu 2
returning
.B None
or 0, or calling
.B sys.exit()
with no code, is status 0;
.IP \(bu
returning an integer, or calling
.BI sys.exit( n )
or
.BI darq.exit( n )\fR,
is that status;
.IP \(bu
anything else, including an uncaught exception, is status 1, with a
description of the failure (the traceback, for an exception).
.PP
.B darq.exit()
can be called from any of the application's threads: it ends the main
thread by raising
.B SystemExit
in it, so its cleanup code runs.
.PP
Any p-calls the application made before it finished are sent first.
.B pyloader
then closes its side of the connection, waits for the p-kernel to
close its side, and exits, even if the application left other threads
running.
.PP
A killed application is stopped by raising
.B SystemExit
in the main thread; any p-call it is blocked in is abandoned.
If the application does not stop within a second (for example, because
it is blocked in native code, such as an idle Qt event loop),
.B pyloader
exits immediately with status 1.
.PP
If the p-kernel refuses the RUN_REQUEST, for instance because it does
not recognise
.IR dpid ,
.B pyloader
logs an error and exits with status 1, without starting the
application.
.PP
If the p-kernel closes the connection while the application is running,
.B pyloader
logs
.RB \(lq "Disconnected by p-kernel: exiting." \(rq,
stops the application, and exits with status 1.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I p-kernel-port
TCP port on which the p-kernel is listening.
.TP
.I dpid
DarqOS process identifier allocated to this process by the p-kernel.
.TP
.I parent-dpid
DarqOS process identifier of the process that requested the spawn, or
0 if it was started by the p-kernel itself.
.TP
.I executable-path
Directory containing the application's
.I main.py
file.
It is added to the front of the module search path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Must allow the
.B darq
package to be imported.
.BR pkernel (8)
sets this when it spawns the loader.
.SH EXIT STATUS
When the application finishes,
.B pyloader
exits with the application's status, if it is from 0 to 255, or 1
otherwise.
Otherwise:
.TP
0
The application was killed by
.BR kill_process .
.TP
1
The p-kernel refused to run the process or closed the connection, the
application could not be stopped, or usage help was requested.
.TP
42
The wrong number of arguments was given.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Log messages are written to standard error.
.SH BUGS
If no p-kernel is listening on
.IR p-kernel-port ,
.B pyloader
exits with a Python traceback rather than an error message.
.PP
Asking for usage help exits with status 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkernel (8)
